# Infrastructure Addressing

Critical infrastructure uses predictable IP addresses so that services remain reachable after system reboots, upgrades, and network changes.

| Device | Hostname | IP Address | Role | Addressing |
|---|---|---:|---|---|
| pfSense | pfSense | `10.0.0.1` | Router / Firewall / VPN Gateway | Static |
| Cisco Switch | SW1 | `10.0.0.2` | Managed Layer 2 Switch | Static |
| Proxmox | pve | `10.0.0.5` | Virtualization Host | Static |
| Domain Controller | DC1 | `10.0.0.6` | AD / DNS / DHCP | Static |
| Wazuh Server | wazuh01 | `10.0.0.7` | SIEM | Static |
| Nessus | Nessus | `10.0.0.8` | Vulnerability Scanner | Planned |
| Client01 | Client01 | `10.0.0.100` | Domain-Joined Windows Client | Client Address |
| Jump PC | Jump PC | `10.0.0.101` | Administrative Workstation | Administrative Client |

The lower portion of the subnet is primarily reserved for infrastructure systems.

This makes important devices easier to identify during administration and troubleshooting.

