# Static vs Dynamic Addressing

The lab uses a combination of static and dynamic addressing.

## Static Addressing

Static addresses are used for critical infrastructure.

Examples include:

```text
pfSense
SW1
Proxmox
DC1
Wazuh
```

These systems must remain at known locations because other devices and services depend on them.

## Dynamic Addressing

DHCP is appropriate for systems where the exact address is less important.

Examples include:

```text
Domain workstations
Temporary lab systems
Test machines
Additional client devices
```

This reduces the amount of manual configuration required as the lab grows.

